# Joust Through targets an attacking or blocking creature only (CR 506.4). Bot1's Isamaru attacks on turn 3 and Bot2's first
# Ornithopter (0/2) blocks it. Before the attack nothing is in combat, so a cast at Bot2's Ornithopter or Bot1's own Isamaru is not
# offered; once Isamaru attacks, the unblocking second Ornithopter and a Bot1 creature that is not attacking are still refused,
# while the blocker is a legal target (positive control), dies to the 3 damage, and Bot1 gains 1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Isamaru, Hound of Konda
Memnite
Joust Through
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Isamaru, Hound of Konda.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Hand.Joust Through.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1)
! Bot1.Hand.Joust Through.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Isamaru, Hound of Konda)
Bot1.Attack(Isamaru, Hound of Konda > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter#1 > Isamaru, Hound of Konda)
! Bot1.Hand.Joust Through.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2)
! Bot1.Hand.Joust Through.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite)
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Joust Through.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Life = 21
Bot1.Graveyard = Joust Through
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
